---
description: Strict React Native Expo implementation rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You MUST strictly follow these rules when generating, modifying, or suggesting code for this React Native (Expo) project. Do not ignore any rule.

==================================================
0. CODE ANALYSIS FIRST (MANDATORY)
==================================================
- ALWAYS analyze the existing codebase before writing any code.
- Understand:
  - Folder structure
  - Component patterns
  - State management
  - Map integration approach
- Identify reusable components, hooks, and services.
- DO NOT write or modify code before analysis is complete.

==================================================
1. CONFIRMATION BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION (MANDATORY)
==================================================
- BEFORE making any change:
  - Explain what will be done
  - Explain why it is needed
- Provide options:
  1. Proceed
  2. Modify approach
  3. Cancel
- DO NOT implement without user approval.

==================================================
2. CONTROLLED EXECUTION
==================================================
- Break implementation into small steps.
- Ask confirmation after each major step.
- Do NOT perform large multi-file changes at once.

==================================================
3. SAFE INTEGRATION WITH EXISTING CODEBASE
==================================================
- Do NOT modify existing working code automatically.
- Apply rules ONLY to:
  - New code
  - Explicitly approved changes
- Do NOT:
  - Rename existing variables/classes
  - Move files/folders
  - Change architecture
UNLESS explicitly approved.

==================================================
4. NON-DESTRUCTIVE DEVELOPMENT
==================================================
- Ensure new changes do NOT break existing functionality.
- Maintain backward compatibility.

==================================================
5. INCREMENTAL REFACTORING
==================================================
- Suggest improvements first.
- Refactor only after approval.
- Perform changes step-by-step.

==================================================
6. CHANGE PREVIEW (MANDATORY)
==================================================
- Before changes:
  - Show what will change
  - List impacted files
  - Mention risk level

==================================================
7. PROJECT STRUCTURE (STRICT)
==================================================
src/
  components/
  screens/
  hooks/
  services/
  utils/
  constants/
  navigation/
  store/
  theme/

- Do NOT introduce unnecessary folders.

==================================================
8. COMPONENT DESIGN
==================================================
- Use functional components only.
- Use React Hooks.
- Keep components small and reusable.

==================================================
9. REUSABILITY
==================================================
- Extract reusable UI → components
- Extract reusable logic → hooks/services

==================================================
10. NO DUPLICATION
==================================================
- NEVER duplicate logic or UI.
- Always reuse existing code if available.

==================================================
11. NAMING (STRICT)
==================================================
- Use meaningful names:
  - lat ❌ → pickupLatitude ✅
- Components → PascalCase
- Variables → camelCase

==================================================
12. CODE STRUCTURE
==================================================
- Keep code modular and clean.
- Follow separation of concerns.

==================================================
13. NO OVER-ENGINEERING
==================================================
- Do NOT introduce unnecessary abstraction.
- Keep solutions simple.

==================================================
14. COMMENTS
==================================================
- Only for complex logic.
- Avoid obvious comments.

==================================================
15. STYLING
==================================================
- Use StyleSheet or project styling system.
- Avoid inline styles unless necessary.

==================================================
16. PERFORMANCE
==================================================
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders.
- Use memoization where needed.

==================================================
17. STATE MANAGEMENT
==================================================
- Follow existing state pattern.
- Do NOT introduce new libraries.

==================================================
18. API HANDLING
==================================================
- APIs must be in services/.
- No direct API calls in components.

==================================================
19. ERROR HANDLING
==================================================
- Use try/catch.
- Show user-friendly errors.

==================================================
20. NAVIGATION
==================================================
- Follow existing navigation structure.

==================================================
21. NO HARDCODING
==================================================
- Use constants/.
- Avoid hardcoded URLs/keys.

==================================================
22. CLEAN CODE
==================================================
- Remove unused imports.
- No commented-out code.

==================================================
23. DEPENDENCIES
==================================================
- Use existing libraries.
- Prefer Expo-compatible packages.

==================================================
24. MAP INTEGRATION (STRICT)
==================================================
- Use one map provider only.
- Prefer react-native-maps (Expo compatible).
- Do NOT mix map libraries.

==================================================
25. LOCATION HANDLING
==================================================
- Use Expo Location API.
- Handle permission denied & errors.

==================================================
26. PICKUP & DROP FLOW
==================================================
- Separate pickup and drop logic.
- Use reusable components:
  - LocationSearchInput
  - MapMarker

==================================================
27. ROUTE & DIRECTIONS
==================================================
- Route logic must be in services/.
- Store:
  - distance
  - duration
  - polyline

==================================================
28. MAP UI RULES
==================================================
- Show:
  - Pickup marker
  - Drop marker
  - Driver marker
- Optimize rendering.

==================================================
29. DRIVER TRACKING
==================================================
- Handle via polling or real-time updates.
- Avoid UI flickering.

==================================================
30. REAL-TIME STATE
==================================================
- Use centralized state for ride + driver.

==================================================
31. ANIMATION & UX
==================================================
- Smooth transitions for map updates.

==================================================
32. SECURITY
==================================================
- Do not expose API keys.
- Use environment variables.

==================================================
33. NO ASSUMPTIONS
==================================================
- Do not assume missing logic.
- Follow existing patterns only.

==================================================
34. MODIFY > CREATE
==================================================
- Prefer modifying existing code when safe.

==================================================
35. UTILITY DISCIPLINE
==================================================
- Avoid generic names (Utils, Helper).
- Use domain-specific naming.

==================================================
36. DATABASE/API EFFICIENCY
==================================================
- Avoid unnecessary API calls.
- Optimize requests.

==================================================
37. TESTABILITY
==================================================
- Keep code loosely coupled.

==================================================
38. FINAL VALIDATION (MANDATORY)
==================================================
Before output:
- Code analyzed
- Confirmation taken
- No duplication
- Existing code untouched unless approved
- Clean, optimized, maintainable
